# wined3d: Don't add buffer views to the buffer object users list when buffer textures are unsupported.
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/12713 state=merged
# When ARB_texture_buffer_object is unsupported, create_buffer_texture() returns without creating a view, but its callers still add the view to buffer-\>buffer_object-\>users. For a buffer created without initial data, buffer_object is still NULL, so creating a buffer shader resource view dereferences NULL.

This only fixes the crash. Without the extension the view still doesn't work.

With the extension forced off, the d3d11 suite then reaches a second problem: wined3d_unordered_access_view_gl_clear() invalidates every location except WINED3D_LOCATION_BUFFER but never marks that location valid. View creation normally loads it first, which hides this; with no buffer textures it no longer does, so the buffer ends up with no valid location and a later wined3d_buffer_copy() reads from a NULL address. The second commit fixes that.

Tested:

- macOS GL (extension hidden with a test-only patch): a D3D11 program creating a buffer SRV over a buffer with no initial data. Master crashes with a page fault at address 0 with the extension off, and runs to completion with it on. With this series it runs to completion in both cases.
- Linux (Mesa llvmpipe, Xvfb), extension available: d3d11, d3d10core and d3d9 device give identical results for master, the first commit and both commits (d3d11 562467 tests, 0 failures; d3d10core 195827 tests, 0 failures; d3d9 device has the same single failure everywhere).
- Linux, extension forced off: d3d11 crashes with "Unexpected locations 0" with only the first commit, and runs to completion with both.
- d3d8 (i386 under qemu, extension on and off, master / first commit / both): stateblock and visual pass with 0 failures in every run. The device test aborts the same way on master (Xvfb has no mode switching), so it gives no result.

Not tested:

- With the extension forced off the views are not functional, and I did not try to make them so: d3d10core finishes with 112 failures and d3d11 with 590, all in tests that create and read a buffer SRV or U
